questions.question:
The incident: a database backup with auth.refresh_tokens leaked, and its tokens worked. A proposed fix in review:

-  if (!row || row.token !== presented) return { ok: false, reason: "unknown" };
+  if (!row || !timingSafeEqual(Buffer.from(row.token), Buffer.from(presented))) {
+    return { ok: false, reason: "unknown" };
+  }

"Constant-time comparison closes the leak."

Statement: "After this change, a token copied from that backup stops working."
